# Build context for the container images whose `image_build_context` is the
# repository root — the one Bun lockfile lives there, so an image that runs a
# frozen install has to see it (poc/cloudflare-runtime-probe).
#
# Docker sends the whole context to the daemon, so keep evidence, credentials,
# installed dependencies and build output out of it. The Dockerfiles copy only
# the manifests, the lockfile and their own sources, so nothing here is needed
# by a build; excluding a path can only make the context smaller.
#
# Every pattern excludes: there are no `!` re-inclusions, so the order of the
# lines does not matter and a new source directory is included by default
# rather than silently dropped.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
data/
**/node_modules/
**/.wrangler/
**/dist/
**/dist-evidence/
**/dist-production/
**/__pycache__/
**/.ruff_cache/
# Local secrets never reach an image layer, even when one is left in a checkout.
**/.dev.vars
**/*.cred
**/*.pem
**/*.key
